    "text": "An object of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed at right angles to the principal axis of a mirror of radius of curvature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> such that its image is virtual, erect and has a length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. What kind of mirror it is and also determine the position of the object?",
